Author: Sanzhar <sanzhar@Sanzhars-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date:   Fri May 29 13:49:46 2026 +0100

    feat(quantbook): 6.4-3d Step 5 (IDE) -- trust-gated UDF worker injection + CellDiagnostic tooltips + error-code allowlist
    
    The IDE side of 6.4-3d (engine side: pollEvents napi binding + worker no-stderr
    robustness, engine commit 1e182a2fad3 on feat/quantbook-engine). Builds the
    contract + helper + renderer surface; the live cellGridPanel still runs on
    CollabSession, so wiring the owning Session + a live pollEvents loop into the
    panel is filed-forward (its own increment).
    
    - types.ts: PythonWorkerConfigJson + setUdfWorker(config) + pollEvents(cursor) on
      SessionInstance; Event/Diagnostic/Severity/OperationState/CellAddr/EventPage TS
      types mirroring the engine DTOs; +5 QuantbookErrorCode union members
      (worker_spawn_failed, worker_handshake, worker_untrusted_workspace,
      invalid_state, session_busy); diagnostic? on the QuantbookCellSnapshot entry.
    - session.ts: the same 5 codes in KNOWN_QUANTBOOK_ERROR_CODE_RECORD
      (compile-enforced parity with the union).
    - loader.ts: setUdfWorker + pollEvents added to the Session.prototype shape check.
    - udfWorker.ts (new): planUdfWorkerConfig (PURE: trust gate ->
      [worker_untrusted_workspace]; interpreter via the quantlab.pythonPath cascade,
      verified >= 3.9 -> [worker_spawn_failed]) + injectUdfWorker (async wrapper; lazy
      vscode/TrustManager imports keep the planner testable without the shim; yields
      before the SYNCHRONOUS, blocking setUdfWorker call -- callers MUST run it off
      the UI path; async-napi AsyncTask filed-forward).
    - cellGridLogic.ts: buildCellDiagnosticMessages (pollEvents page -> per-cell
      message map, sheet-filtered, last-wins) + attachCellDiagnostics (merge onto
      ERROR-valued cells only, so a recovered cell drops the stale tooltip; pure).
    - cellGridHtml.ts: renderRows adds an escapeHtml'd title= tooltip when a cell has
      a diagnostic, KEEPING the #CALC!/#TIMEOUT! text.
    - tests: new quantbook-udf-worker.test.ts (error-code parity, planUdfWorkerConfig
      gates, both diagnostics helpers -- 16 cases, no FFI/vscode);
      quantbook-roundtrip.test.ts fake-Session prototype updated for the 2 new
      loader-checked methods.
    
    Verified: tsc --noEmit clean; quantbook mocha 458/458 (incl. the cdylib-backed
    Session smoke against the 6.4-3d engine build).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

